16477
ADDENDA <Act No. 16477, Aug. 20, 2019>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force 6 months after the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Transitional measures concerning sale of liquefied petroleum gas)
(1) A person who has applied for or obtained permission for the liquefied petroleum gas pipeline network supply business under the previous provisions as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed to have applied for or obtained permission for the liquefied petroleum gas pipeline network supply business, which is a type of liquefied petroleum gas collective supply business, under the amended provisions of subparagraph 6-2 of Article 2 or the provisions of Article 5(1).
(2) A person who supplies liquefied petroleum gas to facilities, other than those referred to in paragraph (1), that were installed under the previous provisions as at the time this Act enters into force and that fall within the definition of liquefied petroleum gas pipeline network supply facilities under the amended provisions of subparagraph 6-2 of Article 2 shall obtain permission for liquefied petroleum gas pipeline network supply business, which is a type of liquefied petroleum gas collective supply business, under subparagraph 6-2 of Article 2 and Article 5(1) within 6 months from the date this Act enters into force.
Article 3 (Transitional measures concerning acting on behalf of gas supplier to perform safety control for gas-using facilities)
A person who acts on behalf of a gas supplier to perform part of safety control for gas-using facilities in accordance with the safety control regulations referred to in Article 31 under the previous provisions as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed a person who acts on behalf of a gas supplier to perform safety control for gas-using facilities in accordance with the amended provisions of Article 30-2.
Article 4 (Transitional measures concerning construction supervision)
(1) A liquefied petroleum gas pipeline supplier who has obtained the safety verification under the previous provisions as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed verified under the amended provisions of Article 36-2.
(2) A liquefied petroleum gas pipeline supplier subject to safety verification under the previous provisions as at the time this Act enters into force shall undergo construction supervision under the amended provisions of Article 36-2.

